  <bib:Article rdf:about="#maferw">
    <z:itemType>conferencePaper</z:itemType>
    <dc:title>MaFeRw: Query Rewriting with Multi-Aspect Feedbacks for Retrieval-Augmented Large Language Models</dc:title>
    <dc:date>2025</dc:date>
    <z:url>https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/34732</z:url>
    <dc:identifier>DOI: 10.1609/aaai.v39i24.34732</dc:identifier>
    <z:extra>发表状态：AAAI 2025 Technical Track，正式同行评审论文。阅读优先级：P0/P1。它做了什么：用 gold 文档相似、排名、生成答案和人工改写等多方面奖励训练 query rewriter。它没做什么：强监督、无长期经验卡和明确 NOOP/伤害门。GrowRAG 必学：检索、证据、答案与改写相似度是不同反馈，不能压成一个不透明 R。</z:extra>
    <bib:authors><rdf:Seq>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Yujing</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Wang</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Hainan</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Zhang</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Liang</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Pang</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Binghui</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Guo</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Hongwei</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Zheng</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Zhiming</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Zheng</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq></bib:authors>
    <dcterms:isPartOf><bib:Proceedings><dc:title>Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Volume 39, Issue 24</dc:title></bib:Proceedings></dcterms:isPartOf>
  </bib:Article>

  <bib:Article rdf:about="#adaqr">
    <z:itemType>conferencePaper</z:itemType>
    <dc:title>Adaptive Query Rewriting: Aligning Rewriters through Marginal Probability of Conversational Answers</dc:title>
    <dc:date>2024</dc:date>
    <z:url>https://aclanthology.org/2024.emnlp-main.746/</z:url>
    <dc:identifier>DOI: 10.18653/v1/2024.emnlp-main.746</dc:identifier>
    <z:extra>发表状态：EMNLP 2024 Main，正式同行评审论文。阅读优先级：P1。它做了什么：不用 passage relevance 标签，以 top-k 文档条件下答案的边际概率评价 rewrite candidate，并用 DPO 对齐。它没做什么：面向对话改写训练，不做运行时历史经验复用。GrowRAG 必学：无文档 gold 时的弱监督 proxy，但必须在有 gold 的 held-out 数据上验证其是否识别 harmful reuse。</z:extra>
    <bib:authors><rdf:Seq>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Tianhua</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Zhang</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Kun</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Li</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Hongyin</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Luo</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Xixin</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Wu</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>James R.</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Glass</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Helen M.</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Meng</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq></bib:authors>
    <dcterms:isPartOf><bib:Proceedings><dc:title>Proceedings of the 2024 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing</dc:title></bib:Proceedings></dcterms:isPartOf>
    <bib:pages>13444–13461</bib:pages>
  </bib:Article>

  <bib:Article rdf:about="#retpo">
    <z:itemType>conferencePaper</z:itemType>
    <dc:title>Ask Optimal Questions: Aligning Large Language Models with Retriever’s Preference in Conversation</dc:title>
    <dc:date>2025</dc:date>
    <z:url>https://aclanthology.org/2025.findings-naacl.328/</z:url>
    <dc:identifier>DOI: 10.18653/v1/2025.findings-naacl.328</dc:identifier>
    <z:extra>发表状态：Findings of NAACL 2025，正式同行评审，但不是 NAACL Main。阅读优先级：P1。它做了什么：收集目标 retriever 对 41 万余 query rewrites 的真实检索偏好，并训练小模型对齐。它没做什么：没有 reliability/applicability 分离、卡片生命周期或 harmful reuse。GrowRAG 必学：经验有效性依赖 retriever；跨环境复用必须显式检查 capability/fingerprint。</z:extra>
    <bib:authors><rdf:Seq>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Chanwoong</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Yoon</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Gangwoo</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Kim</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Byeongguk</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Jeon</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Sungdong</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Kim</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Yohan</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Jo</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Jaewoo</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Kang</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq></bib:authors>
    <dcterms:isPartOf><bib:Proceedings><dc:title>Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: NAACL 2025</dc:title></bib:Proceedings></dcterms:isPartOf>
    <bib:pages>5914–5936</bib:pages>
  </bib:Article>

  <bib:Article rdf:about="#self_multi_rag">
    <z:itemType>conferencePaper</z:itemType>
    <dc:title>Learning When to Retrieve, What to Rewrite, and How to Respond in Conversational QA</dc:title>
    <dc:date>2024</dc:date>
    <z:url>https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-emnlp.622/</z:url>
    <dc:identifier>DOI: 10.18653/v1/2024.findings-emnlp.622</dc:identifier>
    <z:extra>发表状态：Findings of EMNLP 2024，正式同行评审，但不是 EMNLP Main。阅读优先级：P1。它做了什么：将 conversational context 下的是否检索、如何总结/改写、返回 passage 是否相关和如何回答分成控制步骤。它没做什么：无跨题经验卡、条件伤害和 BASE/REUSE 配对。GrowRAG 必学：controller 决策与 query transform/generation 应分开；一个模型可扮演多角色但协议必须解耦。</z:extra>
    <bib:authors><rdf:Seq>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Nirmal</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Roy</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Leonardo F. R.</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Ribeiro</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Rexhina</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Blloshmi</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person><foaf:givenName>Kevin</foaf:givenName><foaf:surname>Small</foaf:surname></foaf:Person></rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq></bib:authors>
    <dcterms:isPartOf><bib:Proceedings><dc:title>Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: EMNLP 2024</dc:title></bib:Proceedings></dcterms:isPartOf>
    <bib:pages>10604–10625</bib:pages>
  </bib:Article>

